      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Ceremonies are what a people DOES —",
          "not now, not once, but as custom.",
          "Swahili has a tense for exactly that:",
          "hu-, and it takes NO who-bead at all.",
          "",
          "   Waswahili husherehekea harusi",
          "   kwa siku nyingi.",
          "   Swahili people celebrate weddings",
          "   over many days.",
          "",
          "   Wageni huja na zawadi.",
          "   Guests customarily bring gifts.",
          "",
          "Hear the custom tense:             Press 1"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Waswahili husherehekea harusi. Wageni huja na zawadi."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "hu- against -na-: habit against now.",
          "",
          "   Yeye hunywa chai.",
          "   He (habitually) drinks tea.",
          "",
          "   Anakunywa chai sasa.",
          "   He is drinking tea right now.",
          "",
          "Hear the pair:                     Press 1",
          "",
          "Because hu- drops the who-bead, the",
          "doer must be named or known — context",
          "carries what the prefix no longer",
          "does. You have met hu- quietly in",
          "example sentences since tier 2; now",
          "it is yours."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Yeye hunywa chai. Anakunywa chai sasa."
        }
      }
    ]
  },
